.TH FIGLET 1 "June 2026" "FIGdriver\-rs 0.5" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
figlet \- render text as ASCII art banners using FIGfont files
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B figlet
[options] [message]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B figlet
is a command\-line tool that renders text as large ASCII art banners using
FIGfont (\fB.flf\fR) or TOIlet (\fB.tlf\fR) font files. It is a Rust
implementation of the FIGfont 2 renderer, powered by the FIGdriver library.
.PP
The tool supports multiple layout modes (kerning, smushing, overlap, full
width), bidirectional text (left\-to\-right and right\-to\-left), word wrapping
with configurable alignment, and character mapping via control files (.flc).
.PP
When a message is provided as arguments, it is rendered directly. If no
message is given, input is read from standard input.
.SH OPTIONS
.B figlet
processes options from left to right; when conflicting options are given,
the last one takes effect.
.TP
.B "\-f, \-\-font"
.IR fontfile
Select the font to use. The
.B .flf
or
.B .tlf
suffix may be omitted. The font is looked up in the font directory set by
\fB\-d\fR. Defaults to
.IR standard.flf .
.TP
.B "\-d, \-\-fontdir"
.IR fontdirectory
Set the font search directory. Defaults to
.IR /usr/share/figlet .
.TP
.B "\-c, \-\-center"
Center output horizontally within the output width.
.TP
.B "\-l, \-\-left"
Flush\-left alignment.
.TP
.B "\-r, \-\-right"
Flush\-right alignment.
.TP
.B "\-x, \-\-default\-align"
(default) Align according to print direction: left for left\-to\-right, right
for right\-to\-left.
.TP
.B "\-t, \-\-terminal\-width"
Query the terminal for its current width and use it as the output width. Falls
back to 80 if the terminal size is unavailable.
.TP
.B "\-w, \-\-width"
.IR cols
Set the output width in columns. This determines where wrapped lines break
and how centered output is padded. Defaults to 80.
.TP
.B "\-S, \-\-smush"
Force smushing: adjacent characters overlap according to their smush parameters.
.TP
.B "\-s, \-\-smush\-default"
Use the font's own default layout mode for each character.
.TP
.B "\-o, \-\-overlap"
Overlap mode: characters overlap but do not smush.
.TP
.B "\-k, \-\-kern"
Kerning mode: adjacent characters are kerned (trimmed) but do not overlap.
.TP
.B "\-W, \-\-full\-width"
Full width mode: characters are rendered at their full declared width with no
smushing or kerning.
.TP
.B "\-m, \-\-layout\-mode"
.IR mode
Override the font's layout mode with an integer. 0 = kern, \-1 = full width,
\-2 = smush default, any positive value = custom mode.
.TP
.B "\-p, \-\-paragraph"
Paragraph mode. Input newlines are collapsed into spaces within a paragraph; a
blank line terminates the paragraph and forces a break.
.TP
.B "\-n, \-\-normal"
(default) Normal mode. Each input newline produces a separate output line.
.TP
.B "\-L, \-\-left\-to\-right"
Force left\-to\-right print direction.
.TP
.B "\-R, \-\-right\-to\-left"
Force right\-to\-left print direction.
.TP
.B "\-X, \-\-font\-direction"
(default) Use the print direction declared by the font file.
.TP
.B "\-C, \-\-control"
.IR controlfile
Load a control file (.flc) for character mapping. May be repeated; control
files are applied in the order given.
.TP
.B "\-I, \-\-infocode"
.IR num
Print metadata for infocode
.I num
(0\-5) and exit:
.RS
.TP
.B 0
Copyright notice and version string.
.TP
.B 1
Version encoded as an integer (major*10000 + minor*100 + patch).
.TP
.B 2
Default font directory.
.TP
.B 3
Default font name (suffix stripped).
.TP
.B 4
Output width.
.TP
.B 5
Supported FIGfont format identifiers (always "flf2 tlf2").
.RE
.TP
.B "\-v, \-\-version"
Print the version and exit.
.TP
.B "\-h, \-\-help"
Print usage information and exit.
.SH EXAMPLES
.PP
Render text with the default font:
.RS
.nf
figlet Hello
.RE
.PP
Render text with a specific font and center\-aligned output:
.RS
.nf
echo "FIGdriver\-rs" | figlet \-c \-f slant
.RE
.PP
Use a custom font and control file:
.RS
.nf
figlet \-f standard \-C slip "Hello"
.RE
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B FIGLET_FONTDIR
If set, use the given directory as the default font search directory, instead
of
.IR /usr/share/figlet .
This can be overridden with
.BR \-d .
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /usr/share/figlet
Default directory searched for fonts and control files.
.SH BUGS
Report bugs at <https://github.com/cmatsuoka/figdriver-rs/issues>.
.SH AUTHORS
